  "id": "pyramidotomy",
  "term": "pyramidotomy",
  "definition": "Pyramidotomy is a procedure that exposes the medullary pyramid in the brainstem and cuts or lesions it. In this source, the term refers to creating a controlled injury of the pyramid for experimental study of motor deficits.",
